From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:22:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ios): the band's bar and the picture shape, checked

- companion_layout.h: the standing bar's canvas is placed by the art
  window's own middle (1016), so the window's 952..1080 span lands on its
  rectangle; the harness asserts both ends.
- DmLayout.h: "auto" clamps to loader.c's 0.9..2.4 range in both
  orientations, so a shape the loader would refuse falls back to 16:9.
- t_touch.c: the mapping cases use points off the middle and the edges,
  where a scale shows, and add a 16:9 case that must not map.
- DuoHarnessTests.m: the docking case reuses one pad, so it checks the
  arrangement's effect rather than a fresh view's default.
- The game note and the two setting references follow the new "auto" and
  the loader's range.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the review of the three patches before it found the standing bar's canvas
placed by 1019.5 while the art window's own middle is 1016, "auto" missing
loader.c's 0.9 lower clamp, and two tests that pass without the code doing the
work (a touch on an edge, a fresh pad per arrangement); this fixes all four and
brings the game note and the two setting references along.
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion or the picture shape

